# ---------------- RULES / LIMITS / FAILURE ----------------
R('L',"Potion cool-down (potion sickness)","After any potion the drinker has a cool-down; taking another before it ends inflicts Poisoned.","B1 ch24","V cite B1 ch24","W:Potion","taking another of any kind before the countdown expires inflicts the Poisoned status effect.")
R('L',"Potion sickness length","Cool-down length is set by Constitution; mobs get none, NPCs do.","B1 ch25; B3 ch7","V cite B1 ch25","W:Potion","Its length is set by Constitution, so sturdier crawlers recover faster.")
R('L',"Potion sickness exemptions","Healing scrolls have no countdown; Splooge is processed as food-based buff.","B1 ch25; B8 ch95","V cite B1 ch25","W:Potion","Healing scrolls sidestep the system entirely, with no countdown between uses")
R('L',"Potion storage","Potions stack to 999 per slot in time-locked storage and do not degrade; grades Good/Great/Superb, Cosmic separate.","B1 ch5; B3 ch7","V cite B1 ch5","W:Potion","they stack up to 999 per inventory slot in time-locked storage, so a stored potion does not degrade.")
R('L',"Permanent stat potion limit","Stat-buff potions can be taken only a limited number of times; Superb grants up to 4; Cosmic Buff potions are a separate type not bound by that limit.","B3 ch7","V cite B3 ch7","W:Potion","These can only be taken a limited number of times regardless of quality")
R('L',"Stat buff cap per stat","A crawler may drink only two of each stat's buff potion in the dungeon.","B3 ch7","V cite B3 ch7",C,"a crawler may drink only two of each stat's buff potion during their time in the dungeon.")
R('L',"Pets and potions","Standard healing potions/scrolls do not affect pet-class creatures; a purpose-brewed variant is needed.","B2 ch12","V cite B2 ch12","W:Potion","Standard potions and heal scrolls have no effect on pet-class creatures")
R('L',"Thrown potions","Thrown potions work on mobs, not expected on crawlers, should work on NPCs/pets; open question.","B3 ch7","V page cite B3 ch7","W:Potion","Thrown potions work on mobs, are not expected to function on fellow crawlers, and should work on NPCs and pets.")
R('L',"Field vs table brewing","Simple recipes can be made without a table; complex ones need one; attempts can fail.","B2 ch17","V cite B2 ch17",C,"Simple alchemical recipes can be made without a table, while more complex recipes require one; attempts can fail.")
R('L',"Boil / emulsify threshold","Dividing line for needing a table: boiling or higher-difficulty emulsifying.","B2 ch17","V cite B2 ch17","W:Potion","the dividing line is whether the recipe calls for boiling or higher-difficulty emulsifying.")
R('L',"Recipes persist","Brewing a recipe once in the field adds it permanently to the crafting menu.","B2 ch12","V cite B2 ch12","W:Potion","brewing one in the field adds the recipe permanently to the crawler's crafting menu.")
R('L',"System names crafted items","The system names and describes crafted items itself, often mockingly; descriptions are not always accurate.","B1 ch32; B3 ch7","V cite B1 ch32",C,"The system names and describes each crafted item itself, often mockingly.")
R('L',"Table crafting can hurt","Even in a safe room, bad workbench crafting can be physically dangerous (Mordecai's warning).","B3 ch4","V cite B3 ch4","W:Goo-Inator 3000","Being in a saferoom may keep you from dying if you fuck something up at a workbench")
R('L',"Goo-Inator imprecision","Overuse of the imprecise tool lowers item strength and can break it.","B3 ch4","V cite B3 ch4","W:Goo-Inator 3000","using the imprecise tool can lower the strength of the item, so if you use it too much it will break.")
R('L',"Table size limit","Large builds may exceed the size a table can handle.","B3 ch31","V cite B3 ch31",C,"large builds may exceed the size a table can handle")
R('L',"Explosives in safe rooms","Explosives are inert in safe rooms; smoke bombs can still be set off.","B1 ch40; B4 ch18","V cite B1 ch40",C,"Explosives are inert inside safe rooms.")
R('L',"Backpack slows destabilization","Unstable explosives in an equipped backpack destabilize more slowly, not never.","B3 ch13","V cite B3 ch13",C,"Carrying unstable explosives in an equipped backpack slows their destabilization, though it does not stop it.")
R('L',"Infusion instability / Dud","Infusing a tossable makes it inherently unstable; failures leave Dud status.","B4 ch18","V cite B4 ch18","W:Potion","Infusing a tossable renders it inherently unstable")
